{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"profile":1,"footerKeywords":13,"hero":111,"footer":124},{"name":2,"surname":3,"jobPosition":4,"presentationHtml":5,"email":6,"github":7,"linkedin":10},"Alessandro","Quets","Digital Designer & Frontend Developer","\u003Cp>My background is in communication and information design. Over the past three years, I’ve worked with startups in DeFi and crypto, designing interfaces and building the frontend behind them.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>My work has ranged from trading products and design systems to a blockchain rebrand. Across these projects, I’ve been interested in the same challenge: helping people understand and use complex products.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Alongside product work, I’m a teaching assistant in interaction design at Politecnico di Milano.\u003C/p>","alessandroquets@gmail.com",{"label":8,"url":9},"MingoBerlingo","https://github.com/MingoBerlingo",{"label":11,"url":12},"linkedin.com/in/alessandro-quets-07531a3b6","https://www.linkedin.com/in/alessandro-quets-07531a3b6/",[14,19,23,27,31,35,39,43,47,51,55,59,63,67,71,75,79,83,87,91,95,99,103,107],{"id":15,"label":16,"order":17,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c578","UX / UI",0,true,{"id":20,"label":21,"order":22,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c57c","Web Design",1,{"id":24,"label":25,"order":26,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c580","Creative Coding",2,{"id":28,"label":29,"order":30,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c584","Dataviz",3,{"id":32,"label":33,"order":34,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c588","Interaction",4,{"id":36,"label":37,"order":38,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c58c","Svelte",5,{"id":40,"label":41,"order":42,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c590","React",6,{"id":44,"label":45,"order":46,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c594","Branding",7,{"id":48,"label":49,"order":50,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb827","Design Systems",8,{"id":52,"label":53,"order":54,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb82b","Prototyping",9,{"id":56,"label":57,"order":58,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb82f","Frontend",10,{"id":60,"label":61,"order":62,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb833","Accessibility",11,{"id":64,"label":65,"order":66,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb837","TypeScript",12,{"id":68,"label":69,"order":70,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb83b","Component Libraries",13,{"id":72,"label":73,"order":74,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb83f","Motion Design",14,{"id":76,"label":77,"order":78,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb843","Data Storytelling",15,{"id":80,"label":81,"order":82,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea691","Figma",16,{"id":84,"label":85,"order":86,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea699","Information Design",17,{"id":88,"label":89,"order":90,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea69d","Interaction Design",18,{"id":92,"label":93,"order":94,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a1","UI Engineering",19,{"id":96,"label":97,"order":98,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a5","Design Tokens",20,{"id":100,"label":101,"order":102,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a9","AI Workflows",21,{"id":104,"label":105,"order":106,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6ad","DeFi",22,{"id":108,"label":109,"order":110,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6b1","Web3",23,{"greeting":112,"nameLine":113,"introduction":114,"homepageIntroduction":115,"featuredProjects":116,"homepageImages":123},"Hey!","I’m Alessandro Quets.","I’m a Digital Designer & Frontend Developer based in Lecco, Italy 🇮🇹","I care about how an interface looks [eye], how it feels, and how it works.\n\nI shape interactions, build design systems, and carry those decisions into production [components] Working in both Figma [figma] and code [code] lets me keep refining the details as I build.\n\nI can sit in a design review and open a pull request [pull-request] on the same day.",[117,119,121],{"id":118},"6ac8b04e1617bfc2eb4349f3",{"id":120},"6ae9da5d2756dce0f10604ee",{"id":122},"6aad520fe6ebe5c3c1970865",[],{"heading":125,"keywordsHeading":126,"signature":127},"Make it clear.\nMake it feel right.","A few things I work with","In ♥ with pixels"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"suggestedProjects":1,"project":27},[2,16],{"id":3,"slug":4,"title":5,"shortTitle":5,"tagline":6,"year":7,"isFeatured":8,"featuredImage":9,"videoCover":15},"6ac8b04e1617bfc2eb4349f3","berachain","Berachain","Designing the face of a blockchain","2026-04-01T12:00:00.000Z",true,{"previewDataURL":10,"url":11,"alt":12,"width":13,"height":14},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/berachain-cover.png","Berachain landing page hero section",1920,1080,null,{"id":17,"slug":18,"title":19,"shortTitle":20,"tagline":21,"year":22,"isFeatured":8,"featuredImage":23,"videoCover":15},"6ae9da5d2756dce0f10604ee","aura","Aura.money","Aura","Building a social trading app","2025-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",{"previewDataURL":24,"url":25,"alt":26,"width":13,"height":14},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/aura-cover.png","Aura trading app on a phone against a blue sky and clouds",{"id":28,"slug":29,"title":30,"shortTitle":31,"tagline":32,"year":33,"isFeatured":8,"isMinor":34,"client":35,"role":36,"output":37,"featuredImage":38,"videoCover":15,"links":42,"collaborators":43,"contentHtml":44,"createdAt":45,"updatedAt":46},"6aad520fe6ebe5c3c1970865","smilee","Smilee Finance","Smilee","Building a scalable DeFi ecosystem","2025-05-01T12:00:00.000Z",false,"DVRS Studio","UX/UI & Fronted","Web Apps",{"previewDataURL":39,"url":40,"alt":41,"width":13,"height":14},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/smilee-cover.png","Smilee Finance cover",[],[],"\u003Ch1>Overview\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Smilee Finance\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Smilee Finance built DeFi products on Arbitrum and Berachain: options trading, liquid staking, dust swapping, and onchain identity through Berachain's name service. I led the design system and designed the UX/UI across the product suite.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-bento.png\" alt=\"Smilee bento presentation\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>The challenge\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Making Web3 and DeFi accessible\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Institutional-grade financial logic had to become a consumer-friendly interface, while accounting for the specifics of Web3 such as wallets, transaction states, onchain confirmations. At the same time, the products needed a single design language that could scale across the suite without fragmenting the user experience.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-screens.png\" alt=\"Smilee finance apps screenshot\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-2\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-web3-ui-example.png\" alt=\"Swappee token selection\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-wallet-interaction.png\" alt=\"Example of typical web3 interaction with transaction signing through wallet extension\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>Design system\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Closing the gap between design and code\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Smilee's brand is playful, bold, and community-focused, meant to appeal to crypto enthusiasts and non-expert users alike. Building on that identity, I created a scalable design system from scratch, tailored to Smilee's UX and brand, and applied it to every released product.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The Figma file and the Svelte codebase stayed in sync, sharing the same tokens, components, and naming conventions. Thanks to an MCP connection between Figma and the code, I could sketch ideas quickly in Figma, iterate on them, and move the results into code with very little friction. This AI-assisted workflow sped up feature releases and kept the products consistent.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-ui-foundations.png\" alt=\"Smilee UI foundation tokens: colors, spacings and text styles\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-2\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-ui-components-2.png\" alt=\"Smilee UI atom components\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/smilee-ui-components-3.png\" alt=\"Smilee UI molecule components\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>What I learned\u003C/h1>\u003Cp>A design system is a set of decisions and conventions. Components, layouts, and screens are just their visible results. Documenting the reasoning behind those choices is what makes the system usable by both designers and developers.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>","2026-09-18T15:00:31.862Z","2026-10-09T09:34:07.854Z"],"uses":{"params":["slug"],"parent":1}}]}
